 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Negative Index Wrapping Bug:** A common implementation error in wrapping negative indices is using the wrong dimension for the modulo operation. Specifically, `if(x<0){x = resX - ((-x) % resY);}` is incorrect because it uses `resY` instead of `resX` for the x-axis modulo, causing incorrect wrapping along the x-axis [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The sources do not specify behavior for coordinates outside the $[0, resX-1] \times [0, resY-1]$ range other than the wrapping bug example. Standard implementations typically clamp or wrap [G].
